/datum/advclass/mercenary/atgervi
	tutorial = "You are a Varangian of the Gronn Highlands. Warrior-Traders most known for their exploits into the Zybantine Empire, which will be forever remembered by historians."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/atgervi_shaman
	tutorial = "You are a Shaman of the Fjall, The Northern Empty. Shamans are savage combatants who commune with the Divine through ritualistic violence, rather than idle prayer."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/blackoak
	tutorial = "A shady guardian of the Black Oaks. Half mercenary band, half irregular militia fighting in the name of their ancestral elven causes. Thankfully, you are not here today to shed the blood of the Count's men — unless someone pays you to..."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/blackoak_ranger
	tutorial = "A shady ranger of the Black Oaks. Half mercenary band, half irregular militia fighting fighting in the name of ancestral elven causes. Thankfully, you are not here today to shed the blood of the Count's men — unless someone pays you to..."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/blackoak_adept
	tutorial = "A spellblade of the Black Oaks. Half mercenary band, half irregular militia fighting in the name of ancestral elven causes. You have honed the ancient Azurean art of spellbladery - an art that is yours and your people's alone. Thankfully, you are not here today to shed the blood of the Count's men - unless someone pays you to..."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/desert_rider_almah
	tutorial = "You're an Almah - a blade dancer, trained in the arts of spellbladery, an art originating from Raneshan in ancient times. Your people have refined spellbladery into an artform. They call you a bladedancer - for the beautiful, bloody tapestry of magycks and blade you weave out of your foes in battle."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/etrusca_condottiero
	tutorial = "Hailing from the Kingdom of Etrusca, you are a Condotierro - an upstart mercenary, dedicated to leading a group of trained soldiers of fortune oft found in the employ of powerful merchants and lords for your efficiency and grace. Without a war to fight back home, the colder climes of the Kingdom has become a much-needed source of contracts. Afterall, this land is rich in coin yet poor in manpower..."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/gronn
	tutorial = "You are one of many upstarts from Gronn, who sailed from the coastal capital of Danheim to the southern beaches of Pharos in search of a more... honest means of profit than the Sea Raiders of infamy."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/grudgebearer
	tutorial = "Bound by eternal grudges of eons past that have not been forgotten, the Grudgebearers are left to wander the surface, as every other clan has a grudge against you, and you against them. This putrid swampland of a County has also wronged you and your people, you care little for it. Coins are a means to an end -- something you can mine and forge yourself. Trinkets -- made by true smiths, now that will carry respect among your clan. However, such artifacts might not buy you food, or a roof."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/grudgebearer_soldier
	tutorial = "Bound by eternal grudges of eons past that have not been forgotten, the Grudgebearers are left to wander the surface, as every other clan has a grudge against you, and you against them. This putrid swampland of a County has also wronged you and your people, you care little for it. Coins are a means to an end -- something you can mine and forge yourself. Trinkets -- made by true smiths, now that will carry respect among your clan. However, such artifacts might not buy you food, or a roof."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/trollslayer
	extra_context = "Only the dwarves who swore an Oath to the Bull may become Trollslayers." // dwarf exclusive and will force Ravox

/datum/advclass/mercenary/steppesman
	tutorial = "Once serving a Hetmen from the frontiers, you have been rented out as a mercenary in the distant realm of Pharos to bring coin home. There are three things you value most; saigas, freedom, and money."

/datum/advclass/mercenary/warscholar_pontifex
	name = "Naledi Medjai"
	tutorial = "A Naledi Medjai, trained in the discipline of Automagic - enhancement of one's own body through Arcyne Magick. \
		Your fists and your will are the one thing that cannot be deprived from you, handy tools when your homeland is rife with treacherous djinns and humens alike. \
		Where your fists fall short, your wits prevail. Where your magyck falters, your fists answer. \
		And when both are found wanting, the Naledian art of blade conjuration will lend you a Katar to cut demons and humens alike to ribbons."
